  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian Development Investments (ADI) regional Climate Catalyst Window - Investment Capital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is ADI&apos;s investment capital contribution under its regional Climate Catalyst Window, which will crowd-in private sector financing for SMEs and assist in the Indo-Pacific region&apos;s clean energy transition. Under the Climate Catalyst Window, ADI will make investments in ODA-eligible Target Countries predominantly in Southeast Asia, with smaller carve outs for South Asia and Pacific Island countries. The funding cap for the Climate Catalyst Window is $126 million, which will be paid into the ADI trust. The window funding is made up of Bill 1 (technical assistance and fees, $22 million) and Bill 2 (investment capital, $104 million). Bill 1 funding for technical assistance and fees is housed under another program fund. The Climate Catalyst Window will be implemented through DFAT&#x2019;s ADI climate finance strategy. Further information on ADI can be found on its website: https://adi.fund/.</narrative>
  </description>
